# Architecture Rules

## Layering

```
entrypoint → service → repository
```

| Layer | Owns | Must not |
|-------|------|----------|
| Entrypoint | Process bootstrap, orchestration, exit codes | Business scoring formulas; raw DynamoDB calls |
| Service | Business logic, scoring, aggregation | Direct AWS SDK client construction (prefer repos/util) |
| Repository | DynamoDB persistence | Scoring / product decisions |

S3 uploads use shared helpers in `src/util/s3/`.

---

## Boundaries

### MUST

- [ ] Keep signal code under `src/signals/<signal>/`
- [ ] Put per-signal services under `src/services/<signal>/`
- [ ] Put per-signal repositories under `src/repositories/<signal>/`
- [ ] Share cross-signal job orchestration via `src/signals/shared-job-signal-orchestration/`
- [ ] Share helpers via `src/util/`, constants via `src/constants/`, types via `src/types/`
- [ ] Read config only through `src/config/config.ts`

### MUST NOT

- ❌ Import one signal package from another (`src/signals/amazon` ↛ `src/signals/walmart`)
- ❌ Put business logic in repositories
- ❌ Hardcode table names, bucket names, or regions — use config/env
- ❌ Duplicate sliding-window or job-repo logic — extend generic modules instead

---

## Adding or Changing Signals

When adding a signal, update **all** of:

1. `src/signals/<name>/entrypoint.ts` (+ calculation modules)
2. `src/services/<name>/` (if needed)
3. `src/repositories/<name>/` (if needed)
4. `src/types/` and `src/constants/` as needed
5. `dev/runners/<name>.dev.ts`
6. Webpack/`SIGNAL_TYPE` build path
7. `cloudformation/` task definitions and DynamoDB tables
8. `docs/SIGNALS.md`, `docs/ENVIRONMENT.md`, `.env.example`
9. Tests with ≥80% coverage contribution

---

## Data Flow Reminder

1. Signal task fetches/processes data
2. Persist signal-specific records in DynamoDB
3. Upload versioned results to S3
4. Blockbuster Index task aggregates signal results
5. Publish final index to S3 + DynamoDB
